  "term": "bed-sharing",
  "definition": "Bed-sharing is a sleep arrangement in which a child sleeps in the same bed as a parent or caregiver. In this source, it refers specifically to reactive bed-sharing in preschool children, meaning bed-sharing examined as a response linked with sleep problems or anxiety rather than as a cause of later psychopathology.",
